<title>LEBANON: Lebanon issues money supply statistics.</title>
<headline>Lebanon issues money supply statistics.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lebanon issued on Tuesday the following money supply statistics for the month of March (billions of Lebanese pounds at end of period):</p>
<p>				  M1	   M2	 M3	 M4</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>    March		    1965	15119     30372     35924</p>
<p>    Feb			1803	14658     29692     34996</p>
<p>    Jan			1775	14328     29332     34313</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    Mar			1604	 10513    23843     27386</p>
<p>    Feb			1585	 10366    23756     27201</p>
<p>    Jan			1516	 10092    23162     26549</p>
<p>The Bank defined the aggregates as follows:</p>
<p>M1 -- Currency in circulation + Demand deposits</p>
<p>M2 -- M1 + Other deposits in Lebanese pounds</p>
<p>M3 -- M2 + Deposits in F.X.</p>
<p>M4 -- M3 + Treasury bills held by the non-banking system</p>
<p>($1= 1,545.75 Lebanese pounds at end of March)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
